        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: 前边",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "前边 — qiánbian — \"in front; ahead\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "前边是火车站 qiánbian shì huǒchēzhàn — The railway station is up ahead."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The new character, in pieces: 边 (biān) — lì, the foot of 男, inside the walking piece that runs down the left and along the foot of 这 and 进. The next lesson puts it in your hand."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "前边 (qiánbian) is built from 前 'front' and 边 (biān) 'side', both inherited from Middle Chinese, dzen and pen (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription); the dictionary glosses the first 'first, before' and the second 'an edge'."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for asking where things are."
            }
          ]
        },
